  "content_blocks": [
    {
      "block_id": "b00000",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Division of contracts into lots",
      "ordinal": 0,
      "heading_path": [
        "Division of contracts into lots"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00001",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "In: Procure > Contract award and implementation",
      "ordinal": 1,
      "heading_path": [
        "Division of contracts into lots"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00002",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Overview",
      "ordinal": 2,
      "heading_path": [
        "Division of contracts into lots",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00003",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "This regulation allows contracting authorities to award a contract in the form of separate lots; provided that the contract notice indicates whether tenders may be submitted for one, for several, or for all of the lots.",
      "ordinal": 3,
      "heading_path": [
        "Division of contracts into lots",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00004",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "When designing the procurement, a contracting authority may decide to limit the number of lots that may be awarded to one bidder, provided that the maximum number of lots per bidder is stated in the contract notice. In such circumstances, the procurement documents must explain how lots will be awarded where the application of the award criteria would result in one bidder being awarded more lots than the maximum number.",
      "ordinal": 4,
      "heading_path": [
        "Division of contracts into lots",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00005",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Where the same bidder is awarded multiple lots, contracting authorities may award contracts combining some or all of the lots provided that the possibility of doing so has been set out in the procurement documents.",
      "ordinal": 5,
      "heading_path": [
        "Division of contracts into lots",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00006",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "To the extent that a contracting authority decides not to award a contract in the form of several lots, it must explain the reasons for this decision in either the procurement documents or in the report required as per regulation 84 PCR 2015 (reporting and documentation requirements).",
      "ordinal": 6,
      "heading_path": [
        "Division of contracts into lots",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00007",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Objective at this commercial stage",
      "ordinal": 7,
      "heading_path": [
        "Division of contracts into lots",
        "Objective at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00008",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Contracting authorities should ensure that the award of contracts combining several or all lots is carried out consistently with the requirements stated in the contract notice.",
      "ordinal": 8,
      "heading_path": [
        "Division of contracts into lots",
        "Objective at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00009",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Key considerations at this commercial stage",
      "ordinal": 9,
      "heading_path": [
        "Division of contracts into lots",
        "Key considerations at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00010",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Contracting authorities should:",
      "ordinal": 10,
      "heading_path": [
        "Division of contracts into lots",
        "Key considerations at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00011",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "ensure that any decision to award contracts combining several or all lots must be consistent with the requirements set out in the procurement documents",
      "ordinal": 11,
      "heading_path": [
        "Division of contracts into lots",
        "Key considerations at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00012",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "ensure that the the decision to combine, or not to combine, certain lots is recorded and maintained in the contracting authority’s internal audit trail.",
      "ordinal": 12,
      "heading_path": [
        "Division of contracts into lots",
        "Key considerations at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
